  "observations": [
    "The published tour camera ties the shelter and approximately north–south ironwork to the western approach. The audited footprint clears the nominal carriageway. No modeled buildings or water overlap the footprints.",
    "The graded fixture shows a continuous route from the pedestrian arch toward the clay return. The extended south pier footing reaches the retained terrain even with grading disabled.",
    "The retained road, landcover and water features survive the fit and unloading. The test did not replace any map line or create a terrain cutout.",
    "The grade approximates the photo and retained elevation data. At host terrain resolutions too coarse for the grade blend, part of the northern apron can still be covered by the terrain overlay. Roof details, fine clay surfaces and the unmapped path beyond the gate remain approximate."
